ally I thought that was clear by the leading underscore.\n\nSorry, my comment wasn't clear. With \"use\" above, I'm not talking about `_git_custom_command`, but about GitPython. Reading the \"without the need to figure out, how this is done via GitPython\" part, I'd think \"OK, so ideally I should try to use GitPython when creating GitRepo methods\". But it sounds like, while GitPython use outside GitRepo is the biggest concern, we also want to avoid GitPython **within** GitRepo methods, but to me this comment suggests using GitPython is the preferred way.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1538664364,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNzA0NjkzMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2879#issuecomment-427046932"},"message":"Right, I missed that part of the comment. This should be removed from that comment. Your interpretation is correct, but the comment is outdated. ;-)","files":null}]}